>

  <p>
    When you arrive in London, one of the first things you'll run into is a very British
    catch-22: most banks require a proof of address to open an account — but you can't get
    most proofs of address without a bank account. The good news? There's a way around it,
    and it takes about 10 minutes.
  </p>

  <!-- ── Section 1 ────────────────────────── -->
  <h2>Start here: digital banks</h2>

  <p>
    The fastest way to get a UK bank account is with a digital bank. Both <strong>Monzo</strong>
    and <strong>Starling</strong> are fully-licensed UK banks — authorised and regulated by the
    Financial Conduct Authority (FCA) and protected by the Financial Services Compensation Scheme
    (FSCS) up to <strong>£85,000 per person</strong>. Critically, neither requires proof of address
    to open an account.
  </p>

  <p>What you'll need:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>A <strong>UK phone number</strong> — buy a pay-as-you-go SIM on arrival. Giffgaff, Three and iD Mobile all offer pay-as-you-go with no contract required.</li>
    <li>Your <strong>passport or national ID</strong></li>
    <li>About <strong>10 minutes</strong> — the whole process happens inside the app</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    You'll receive a full UK current account with a sort code and account number. You can receive
    your salary, set up direct debits, and your physical debit card arrives by post within a few
    working days.
  </p>

